@@ -30,3 +30,51 @@ not proof that a generated launch is legal.
 
 This contract does not query CUDA, link TensorIR/CUDA Tile, compile an
 artifact, or launch a kernel.
+
+## CompileRequest v1
+
+`CompileRequest` is the immutable, pointer-free worker payload for program and
+target policy. It value-owns `NvidiaTargetInfo` and `ToolchainIdentity`; the
+latter records the exact PyPTO, TensorIR, CUDA Tile, and LLVM revisions, a
+normalized CUDA toolkit root/version, and the parent-resolved `tileiras` real
+path/version/executable SHA-256. Duplicate target/toolchain revision or toolkit
+fields must agree. The value object requires already-canonical absolute paths;
+the parent remains responsible for resolving symlinks/`realpath` and hashing
+the selected executable before construction. Deserialization performs no
+filesystem lookup.
+
+V1 fixes all three policies to fail-closed values:
+
+- `RequestedArtifactPolicy.CubinOnly` requests native Cubin and permits no
+  fallback artifact;
+- `CompilerPolicy.DeterministicStrict` requires the later compiler bridge to
+  reject ambient or nondeterministic compiler overrides;
+- `VerificationPolicy.Strict` requires strict validation at the later producer
+  and artifact boundaries.
+
+`serialize()` emits canonical MessagePack. `deserialize()` accepts that exact
+form only: malformed input, trailing bytes, missing/duplicate/unknown fields,
+unsupported versions, noncanonical field order, and noncanonical path spelling
+are rejected. V1 caps the payload at 1 MiB and applies schema-sized
+container/string/depth limits before MessagePack allocation. The schema and
+compiler ABI versions are both explicit.
+
+Three domain-separated canonical SHA-256 identities keep unrelated concerns
+out of the byte cache key:
+
+- `byte_compile_identity_digest` includes all codegen resource traits and the
+  exact compiler toolchain, but excludes device ordinal/name/UUID/PCI identity
+  as well as driver version and total global-memory capacity;
+- `loader_compatibility_input_digest` is request-side policy input containing
+  the requested kind, target architecture, and CUDA driver/toolkit versions.
+  It is not a compatibility result; a later artifact must add its actual kind,
+  target, and runtime requirements;
+- `device_autotune_identity_digest` additionally binds physical device
+  identity, driver, and the complete measured resource/capacity traits to the
+  byte identity.
+
+The request has no IR/source region, route switch, schedule or tile constants,
+model/operator identity, compiled bytes, CUDA module/context/stream/handle,
+tensor/workspace pointer, cache, runtime, or plugin state. This data contract
+does not change legacy `ir.compile`, link TensorIR/CUDA Tile, register a
+backend, compile an artifact, or initialize CUDA.
